          "generalFeedback": "ATDD (Acceptance Test-Driven Development) has the whole team — business, developers, and testers — agree on concrete acceptance tests for a requirement before it is built. Those tests are written from the customer/business perspective, express what \"done\" means, and drive the implementation outside-in.",
