          "generalFeedback": "Test X describes end-to-end, customer-visible behaviour agreed with the business — an ATDD acceptance test. Test Y verifies one internal function in isolation — a developer unit test (TDD). Both are valuable and typically coexist: Y is the kind of test written inside Develop to help make X pass.",
          "single": true
